      "after": "  the originals remain snapshot bytes for identity but are never read by Cargo.\n\n**NCP-1 conditional native configuration read and serialization compatibility.** Under the complete actually owned native configuration profile, docs/implementation/m3/snapshot-plan-c/native-config-projection-compatibility-r1/CONTRACT.md and selection.json require complete original UTF8/TOML/ConfigValue conversion before filtering and strip each selected original document's top-level include value before merge and before any include path resolution, metadata inspection or read. Valid converted include data supplies no include-specific grammar or authority; generic document failures retain their actual origin with no new public default. Complete actual stripped-key accounting under unchanged carrier limits is still required; no wildcard/drop/empty-catalog shortcut. The same unit SERIALIZATION.md selects recursive actual table key str Ord insertion, unchanged list order/repeats and one exact pinned locked toml::to_string call with no byte postprocessing; its nine test-only artifact controls/wholeproducerbuild pass. Original Definition associations remain external to file bytes, and actual key-record representation/resource/public routes remain open. Ordinary Cargo behavior and existing CC1-CC5/CENV1/CRA1/NRC1 identities, source populations and file-versus-record digests remain unchanged. Whole owned discovery/definition/path/serializer/parser-resource/public-failure/input/Tool/profile/owner/library/worker/qualification publication and implementation remain open; this selection alone is no full native profile or runtime admission."
